{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":45},"timestamp":1790746075,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":".venv/bin/watcher ask --real --tenant █████████ \"which acquisition ██████ produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\"","title":"real_██████_quality","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-30 10:57:56\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.2s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.2s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.2s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.2s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/cortex/memory/vector_store.py:191: UserWarning: Api key is used with an insecure connection.\r\n  self._client = AsyncQdrantClient(url=self._url, api_key=self._api_key)\r\n  [  1.2s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/qdrant_client/async_qdrant_remote.py:225: UserWarning: Qdrant client version 1.18.0 is incompatible with server version 1.16.3. Major versions should match and minor version difference must not exceed 1. Set check_compatibility=False to skip version check.\r\n  show_warning(\r\n  [ 13.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 13.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 13.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 13.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 13.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.0s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 29.4s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 29.4s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 29.4s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 29.4s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 83.8s]          drafting the report from 8 observation(s)\r\n  [130.2s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [130.2s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause\r\n  [144.1s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 130s over 3 steps, 93,723 tokens, 8 observations gathered, 5 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  OFFLINE is the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st labeled \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 in both closed-won and closed-lost deals, but its \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail values (IMPORT, CRM_UI, EXTENSION, INTEGRATION) show it is a record-creation label, not a marketing channel, so it cannot be \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed as the acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that 'converts.'  [hubspot.closed_won 8c4c550b, hubspot.search 5ecce1ff]\r\n  DIRECT_TRAFFIC shows similar late-stage pipeline presence but has no confirmed closed-won deals yet, so its conversion strength remains unproven rather than ruled out.  [hubspot.pipeline 41f21187]\r\n  Roughly half of all deal records lack any \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 attribution, which limits confidence in any channel-level comparison until data hygiene improves.  [hubspot.closed_won 8c4c550b, hubspot.search 5ecce1ff]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  OFFLINE/IMPORT dominates raw deal volume but is mostly a data-entry artifact, not a channel  (high)\r\n    - \u2588\u2588 of the \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals with a recorded \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 in one sample, and \u2588\u2588-\u2588\u2588 of the closed-lost sample, carry \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588=OFFLINE with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail values like IMPORT, CRM_UI, EXTENSION, or INTEGRATION \u2014 labels that describe how the deal record was created in HubSpot, not a marketing acquisition channel.  [hubspot.search 2d32e9b6, hubspot.search 5ecce1ff]\r\n    - Among the \u2588\u2588 closed-won deals, \u2588 carry \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588=OFFLINE (all with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail IMPORT or INTEGRATION), while \u2588 more have no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 recorded at all, and only \u2588 has a true \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-channel \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588.  [hubspot.closed_won 8c4c550b]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [contradicted] OFFLINE (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588=OFFLINE) is the acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that actually converts to closed-won deals at the highest rate.\r\n      OFFLINE is overwhelmingly the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 bucket in both closed-won and closed-lost populations, and its \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail values (IMPORT, CRM_UI, EXTENSION, INTEGRATION) describe record-creation mechanism rather than a genuine acquisition channel, so it cannot be \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed as a converting marketing \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588; it is a data-entry legacy label covering most of the CRM regardless of outcome.\r\n  [supported] ORGANIC_SEARCH is a genuine acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that converts to closed business, evidenced by the one attributable closed-won deal and its strong, disproportionate share of advanced-stage open pipeline deals.\r\n      ORGANIC_SEARCH is the only non-OFFLINE \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 with a confirmed closed-won example, and it is heavily represented among high-probability, late-stage open deals (decisionmakerboughtin, contractsent), suggesting it is not just generating deal volume but generating deals that progress toward close.\r\n  [inconclusive] DIRECT_TRAFFIC is a comparably strong or better converting \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 than ORGANIC_SEARCH, given its presence among late-stage open deals.\r\n      DIRECT_TRAFFIC appears in decisionmakerboughtin-stage deals in the open pipeline, but has zero closed-won deals in the sample and a much smaller, less certain historical base than ORGANIC_SEARCH, so its eventual close rate cannot yet be measured \u2014 only its pipeline presence, which is not the same as demonstrated conversion.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Prioritize investment in organic search content and SEO, since it is the only channel with both a confirmed closed-won deal and a disproportionate share of late-stage, high-probability open pipeline.\r\n      why: ORGANIC_SEARCH shows the clearest signal of converting past creation into real commercial progress across both historical closed-won data and current pipeline stage distribution.\r\n      [hubspot.search c40d47bc, hubspot.pipeline 41f21187]\r\n  P\u2588 Fix hs_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data hygiene: stop coding CRM-entry mechanisms (IMPORT, CRM_UI, EXTENSION, INTEGRATION) as 'OFFLINE' acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, and require true \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 on deal creation.\r\n      why: Without this, OFFLINE will continue to dominate both won and lost buckets in a way that makes channel-level conversion analysis unreliable.\r\n      [hubspot.search 5ecce1ff, hubspot.search 2d32e9b6]\r\n  P\u2588 Re-run this analysis once more of the current ORGANIC_SEARCH/DIRECT_TRAFFIC pipeline deals actually close, to convert the leading-indicator finding into a confirmed close-rate comparison.\r\n      why: Current support for ORGANIC_SEARCH rests on one closed-won deal plus pipeline stage/probability, not a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 sample of realized outcomes.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 41f21187]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-won and closed-lost \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 fields are heavily null (\u2588\u2588-\u2588\u2588% missing in closed-lost, ~\u2588\u2588% in closed-won), so the true won/lost mix by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 is under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed for whichever channel a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 share of the null-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deals actually belongs to.\r\n  - Both closed-lost queries were truncated at \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching rows respectively, so the full lost population's \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 mix could differ from what the digest and sample show.\r\n  - The open pipeline is a leading indicator, not a closed outcome \u2014 advanced-stage deals \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d from ORGANIC_SEARCH or DIRECT_TRAFFIC have not yet closed and could still be lost, so their probability field (an \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 CRM estimate) is being used as a proxy for eventual close rather than an observed one.\r\n  - OFFLINE/IMPORT \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail values likely represent a bulk historical data migration (many deals created on the same date, 2026-01-05) rather than an ongoing channel, which further weakens any comparison of OFFLINE against live \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 channels.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The evidence shows OFFLINE deals repeatedly paired with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail values IMPORT, CRM_UI, INTEGRATION in both closed-won and closed-lost samples, supporting the record-creation-\r\n- executive_summary[2]: The evidence shows one DIRECT_TRAFFIC deal at decisionmakerboughtin (late-stage) with no closed-won deals visible in this truncated list, but this single deal doesn't establish a b\r\n- executive_summary[3]: The evidence shows many null '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' fields in both samples but never computes an actual proportion of missing-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 records across the full dataset, so the 'roughly half' figure\r\n- findings[0].claims[0]: The truncated evidence only shows a handful of records with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail=IMPORT and doesn't display the full \u2588\u2588\u2588 or \u2588\u2588\u2588-record sets needed to verify the exact \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s \u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\r\n- ... and \u2588 more.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-lost query returned only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching rows, and the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 query only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588; digests over the full set were used for aggregate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s but detailed row-level analysis only covers the returned subset.\r\n  - A \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 share of both closed-won and closed-lost deals have null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail fields, meaning true \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 is unknown for roughly half of all deals in this analysis.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  8c4c550b  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2025-01-01..2026-09-30\r\n  41f21187  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  c40d47bc  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  5ecce1ff  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n  2d32e9b6  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588?\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (144s wall, 142s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      1.1    1%     1.1  no model call\r\n  recall           1    0.029    0%   0.029  no model call\r\n  loop_model       3     71.0   49%    23.7  in 6 out 6,582 cached 25,807\r\n  loop_tools       2     11.6    8%     5.8  no model call\r\n  draft            1     46.4   32%    46.4  in 82,664 out 4,471\r\n  gate             1    0.040    0%   0.040  no model call\r\n  verify           1     11.7    8%    11.7  in 54,997 out 1,888\r\n  sufficiency      1   <0.001    0%  <0.001  no model call\r\n  unmeasured              2.2    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 16%\r\n"]
